# Polaris web components

This repo is a static Shopify-admin mockup for Findter Filter & Search, not an embedded Remix app. Mockup files live under `findter-mockup/`. `Findter.html` redirects to `index.html`. `python3 findter-mockup/assemble.py` rebuilds `index.html` and `app/home.html` from the parts.

## CDN (this mockup)

App Home (`findter-mockup/app/`, assembled into `app/home.html`) loads live Polaris 2.0 RC:

`https://cdn.shopify.com/shopifycloud/polaris-2.0-rc.js`

Add that script in the app iframe `<head>` only (see `app/shell.html`). Do not load `polaris.js` or `polaris-1.js` alongside it. Do not add it to the frozen admin chrome parent page.

## App UI

Use public Polaris web components (`s-*`) for app UI content. The tags are global. Do not import `@shopify/polaris`, `@shopify/polaris-react`, or `@shopify/polaris-web-components`. Add `@shopify/polaris-types` only when a file needs types.

Before writing a tag, look it up on the App Home docs:

- https://shopify.dev/docs/api/app-home
- https://shopify.dev/docs/api/polaris/using-polaris-web-components

App Home is the surface for this mockup. Checkout and customer-account extensions are a different set (they include `s-form`). Do not copy those tags here.

Use `s-page`, `s-section`, `s-stack`, `s-grid`, `s-box`, `s-button`, `s-text`, `s-text-field`, `s-banner`, `s-badge`, `s-table`, and the other public `s-*` elements. Match an App Home pattern when the screen is one: empty state, index table, settings, details, homepage.

## Attributes

- In JSX/TSX, multi-word properties are camelCase: `alignItems`, `borderRadius`, `accessibilityLabel`, `gridTemplateColumns`, `commandFor`. Do not hyphenate them (`align-items`).
- In HTML mockup files, use those same property names. The HTML parser lowercases them (`accessibilitylabel`). `accessibilityLabel` and `accessibilitylabel` are one attribute. Do not switch to CSS kebab-case.
- Slot values stay kebab-case: `slot="primary-action"`.
- Boolean attributes (`disabled`, `loading`, `dismissible`, `required`): in JSX, shorthand or `{true}` / `{false}`. In HTML, presence means true; omit the attribute for false. `disabled="false"` is still true.
- String keyword attributes must be quoted strings: `padding`, `gap`, `direction`, `tone`, `variant`, `size`, `background`, `alignItems`, `inlineSize`. Write `gap="base"`, `variant="primary"`, `tone="info"`. Do not use boolean shorthand or an unquoted identifier. Spacing uses the middle-out scale: `small`, `base`, `large`, and steps such as `small-100` and `large-100`.

## Known gaps

There is no `s-card`. Use `s-section` for a section.

There is no `s-form` in App Home. Use a native `<form data-save-bar>` when the screen needs a save bar, and `data-discard-confirmation` when discard should ask first. This mockup has no App Bridge runtime, so `shopify.toast`, `shopify.loading`, and the save bar do not run here. Still use the native form. Do not build a fake save bar.

## Mockup split

Admin chrome (global nav, top bar) is the existing HTML mock in `findter-mockup/admin/` (`document-head.html`, `admin/chrome/before-frame.html`, `admin/chrome/after-frame.html`), assembled into `index.html`. Shopify does not publish that shell. `s-internal-*` is internal. Leave the chrome mock as it is.

App body is the iframe document: parts in `findter-mockup/app/`, assembled into `app/home.html`. New or replaced app-body UI is public `s-*`.

Other Admin surfaces that are not App Home (for example Theme Editor for the app-embed case) live under `findter-mockup/screens/` as frozen SingleFile pages. Do not run those through `assemble.py`.

The current pages are a SingleFile snapshot. They do not load a Polaris `<script>`. Rendered components are frozen in `<template shadowrootmode="open">`, mixed with legacy `Polaris-*` class markup. The parent page scripts `assemble.py` adds are `components/highlight-features/highlight.js`, `components/master/master.js` and `components/mockup-cases/mockup-cases.js`.

When new markup must register live `s-*` elements, add exactly one script in that document's `<head>`:

`https://cdn.shopify.com/shopifycloud/polaris-2.0-rc.js`

This mockup uses the Polaris 2.0 RC channel (see `app/shell.html`). Do not load `polaris.js` or `polaris-1.js` alongside it. Do not add the script to the frozen admin chrome parent page. Do not copy shadow-root CSS out of the snapshot to imitate a component.

## Styling and copy

Do not restyle Polaris with custom CSS, inline styles, or utility classes on buttons, badges, banners, inputs, or other `s-*` controls. This repo has no Tailwind build. Admin-shell CSS under `findter-mockup/admin/styles/` stays with the chrome mock. `app/styles/polaris-tokens.css` is snapshot theme data; do not add a second theme.

Merchant-facing copy is English for EU merchants. Reuse the wording already in the mockup. Do not invent algorithm, ranking, or model names for merchants.

## When nothing fits

Compose existing `s-*` pieces. Ask before adding a custom control, wrapper, or visual style.

```html
<s-page heading="Search settings">
  <s-section heading="Basic search">
    <s-stack gap="base">
      <s-banner tone="info">Check search relevance details.</s-banner>
      <s-button variant="primary">Search settings page</s-button>
    </s-stack>
  </s-section>
</s-page>
```

```html
<div class="card">
  <button class="Polaris-Button Polaris-Button--variantPrimary">Search settings page</button>
</div>
```
